  "notes": [
    "The universe remains degenerate in the ways integration round 2 recorded, and w107 closes none of them. Two measured findings worth reading beside this gate. First, the v1 rectangle cannot make food: of the 59 authored resource-yield effects at target universe, exactly five sit in a v1 cell and all five route to stone, because terram is the only material-bearing form among the twelve. Every ruleset comparison taken inside the v1 rectangle is therefore an argument about stone. Second, stated carefully because the sloppy version has misled several readers: advanceConstruction and applyLibraryUpkeep both have production callers in world-step.ts and run every tick, so construction is NOT inert. What is measured over 1200 ticks of the reference universe with zero god actions is constructionStoneOwed 0, buildProgressAdded 0, universitiesCompleted 0, against exactly one university -- the seeded academy, already complete. Founding a site is a god action, so with no actions submitted there is nothing to advance and stone is never spent. Those two facts together are why the campaign-plan W90 measurement of a yield-maximising ruleset was null by construction of its arms rather than for want of a mechanism: the arms could only make stone, and stone had nothing to buy.",
    "Measured 2026-08-14 on w70/opening-square merged with origin/main at 769452845f31c33ab7800d3333fcb5c818feef41. NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED, and none needed to be: what moved is the stream registry hash, not a replay. ui/session.json is byte-identical after npm run ui:record -- snapshotHash did not move. balance-gate-ascension-v1 was deliberately NOT re-recorded: it carries the same superseded rngRegistryHash and will refuse for the same reason, but its Actions job is already failing on main at that ref and is marked not required to merge, so re-recording it is a separate decision on a separate failure.",
    "Re-recorded 2026-08-14 on w108/university-fidelity merged with origin/main at 8d2159f. The seven rows that move are the seven this branch reported before the merge, delta for delta and standard error for standard error, so twenty commits of main changed none of the movement: referenceLibraryDepth@denial-warden -4.00 SE (tol 0.375), referenceNodesGained@denial-warden -9.19 SE (tol 0.530), referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter@denial-warden +3.58 SE (tol 0.839), referenceNodesKnown@denial-warden -9.19 SE (tol 0.530), referencePeakPopulation@archivist +5.52 SE (tol 15.75), referencePeakPopulation@permissive-breadth +8.00 SE (tol 2.625), referencePeakPopulation@worship-maximizer +10.29 SE (tol 5.250). balance-gate-v1 and balance-gate-horizon-v1 both PASS on this tree and are deliberately not touched. NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED and no RNG stream was added; ui/session.json was re-recorded by npm run ui:record and its snapshotHash reproduces this branch pre-merge value byte for byte.",
    "Re-recorded 2026-08-14 on the anti-requisites branch MERGED WITH origin/main be446a6 (PR #125). The exclusion pair is unobservable to the two reference gates and observable to the agency gate, which is the whole shape of this re-baseline; the reference gates do carry movement here, but it is #125 and not the pair, established by stripping the excludes arrays and reproducing every reference value byte-identically. Note carried forward from PR #161 and NOT fixed there: rules-raid raids.ts resolves attacker = outbound ? local : rival, and the ephemeral rival built at scenario/src/rival-universe.ts:298 calls KnowledgeSubsystem.fromState WITHOUT the exclusion resolver -- the only production fromState caller that omits it -- so a rival mage stealing on an INBOUND raid is unchecked. That world is discarded when the portal closes, so nothing it acquires persists, but the engagement loot and the RaidRecord metrics derived from it are still reachable. It is a one-argument change and belongs in its own commit."
