  "rationale": "PR #161 (anti-requisites) ships one symmetric exclusion pair in packages/content/data/cell.json: creo-ignem EXCLUDES creo-umbra and back, both halves carrying the same reason and resolution \"destructive\". Recorded from the tree MERGED WITH origin/main be446a6 (PR #125, w108/university-fidelity), not from the branch alone, per the w77 precedent that a competing baseline re-record means taking the measurement from the merged tree. THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BALANCE CLAIM: release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0, and nothing here is one. BYTE-IDENTITY IS ESTABLISHED BY GREPPING FOR NON-ZERO DELTAS, NOT BY READING THE PASS COLUMN -- a row can pass three standard errors while moving a great deal, and this gate has a live example: referenceGrimoires@permissive-breadth moves +19.6 and PASSES at 1.27 SE. NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED. balance-gate-ascension-v1 is deliberately NOT re-recorded: it carries a superseded rngRegistryHash from PR #72, already fails on main for that older and unrelated reason, and balance/README.md marks its job not required to merge, so re-recording it is a separate decision on a separate failure -- the same carve-out the w70/opening-square notes record. THIS FILE (the twenty-year agency gate, worldTickCap 240, 64 runs, 8 strategies round-robin, 90 rows) IS THE ONE THE MECHANIC MOVES, AND IT REFUSED BEFORE READING A METRIC: provenance.contentHash d4e3047657b4fa8a1a74e1d52f9f5c86 -> e8442af2c5f91ae6f80ad9a178e0e451, correctly, because the content did change. The repository owner authorised the re-record. The agency pool permits the FULL GRID, so unlike the reference universe it can reach creo and the pair fires in a real run. 71 of 90 rows are at delta 0.00000. The 19 that moved are 9 pooled aggregates and all 10 permissive-breadth arm rows -- AND NOTHING ELSE, so THE OTHER SEVEN STRATEGIES ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL ACROSS ALL 70 OF THEIR ARM ROWS and the pooled aggregates move only because they pool permissive-breadth. That result survived the merge with #125 unchanged in shape, which is the check worth recording: a competing re-baseline could have moved other arms and turned this from a re-quote into a different finding, and it did not. Headline on the merged tree: referenceNodesKnown@permissive-breadth 68.6250 -> 42.5000, delta -26.1250 (-20.80 SE against k = 3), and referenceNodesGained@permissive-breadth -26.1250 (-20.80 SE). Also referenceKnowledgeInstances@permissive-breadth 1614.38 -> 1013.00 (-27.04 SE), referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter@permissive-breadth 14.6250 -> 5.25000 (-25.00 SE), and moving UPWARD referenceGrimoires@permissive-breadth +19.6250 (1.27 SE, passing) and referencePeakPopulation@permissive-breadth 330 -> 340 (1.27 SE). permissive-breadth was the top-ranked strategy on referenceNodesKnown and is now fourth. That is one authored pair doing what an opposing term is for, aimed at the strategy that had none. Tolerances moved with the values, so the power table in balance/README.md moves in the same commit and BLIND_ARM_LINES is recomputed; gate-power.test.ts enforces both, correctly.",
